This solution generates Fibonacci numbers in order and tests each one for primality, counting the primes until it reaches the n-th. It uses a deterministic Miller-Rabin test, so large Fibonacci numbers are handled quickly.

The first 12 bases (2 through 37) make Miller-Rabin deterministic for numbers below about 3.3e24. For larger numbers it is a very strong probabilistic test, which is fine in practice. To make the test more robust, the code also uses a few extra bases.

